he number of nuclei  and the number of genes detected um but  what's really quite surprising  is that in certain certain areas of  illumination at least  whereas we're detecting you know above  median  so almost 8 000 genes in a sample it was  probably something like  20 or 30 cells and obviously this is  going to depend upon the transcriptional  activity of the cell type that you're  looking at  and other considerations like the  density of the cells and so on but  i can certainly say we're quite pleased  by this and this is an experiment we  plan to do which is essentially a  titration looking at  across different cell types what kind of  sensitivity can we achieve  based on different areas of illumination
 

